01:27:52.098 --> 01:27:55.898
they prompted thousands of problems,
and what they dropped were only the

01:27:55.958 --> 01:28:00.118
positive solutions, that they only
had about a ten percent success rate.

01:28:01.098 --> 01:28:04.858
So we're sort of left guessing, you
know, is there a very jagged boundary

01:28:04.998 --> 01:28:08.438
that we could squint at and say
we can make sense out of that

01:28:08.498 --> 01:28:12.898
distinguishes you know, what did
fall versus what didn't fall?

01:28:13.918 --> 01:28:17.878
I think one of the other dangers is that maybe
the problems which are the safest are ones

01:28:17.918 --> 01:28:21.658
which you look at and it's just
painfully obvious you need a

01:28:21.738 --> 01:28:23.038
really creative new idea.

01:28:24.138 --> 01:28:28.038
You know, because you can sort of tell
that maybe there's a barrier and the

01:28:28.098 --> 01:28:31.598
things that are out there in the literature
just don't seem to fit into that hole.

01:28:32.418 --> 01:28:36.198
But now I think one of the things that's changed
the landscape of math forever is, you know,

01:28:36.838 --> 01:28:40.758
maybe people become a little bit more
secretive with those ideas than they were in

01:28:40.798 --> 01:28:44.738
the past. You know, because once
those ideas are out there, then,

01:28:45.078 --> 01:28:48.998
you know, it might be a lot more
straightforward for AI to be able to

01:28:49.038 --> 01:28:52.758
balance that one new idea, that
missing ingredient, that new tile

01:28:52.998 --> 01:28:56.858
it needs, and be able to fully
exhaustively explore what it can

01:28:56.918 --> 01:29:00.758
reach out of that. So you might be a lot
more protective of your ideas than you

01:29:00.798 --> 01:29:04.158
were in the past. I think
that's also a bit scary because

01:29:04.218 --> 01:29:07.918
traditionally, the mathematics
community has been really open with

01:29:07.978 --> 01:29:11.498
sharing ideas, and that would
be something bad to lose.

01:29:12.098 --> 01:29:16.038
- But that's also because we had this first
through the gate mentality, and I think

01:29:16.098 --> 01:29:17.058
that's also gonna change.

01:29:17.158 --> 01:29:17.558
- That's right.

01:29:17.998 --> 01:29:21.278
- I would prefer that the openness stay and
the first through the gate is what goes.

01:29:21.298 --> 01:29:22.658
- That's right, but that'll take time.

01:29:22.758 --> 01:29:23.198
- It'll take time.

01:29:23.258 --> 01:29:26.958
- Yeah. So that could be an effect, you
know, that's more transient in nature,

01:29:27.138 --> 01:29:30.698
that if we can learn how to value other
things, then maybe that'll go away.

01:29:31.198 --> 01:29:35.118
There are other communities that have models
for how to value contribution, even when it's

01:29:35.178 --> 01:29:39.038
not lionizing one
individual's contribution. So

01:29:39.058 --> 01:29:42.558
it's not that there's not a way forward,
but, you know, that is, in the short term,

01:29:43.258 --> 01:29:46.098
a real roadblock to doing
mathematics the way that we used to

01:29:47.138 --> 01:29:48.818
and enjoying it the same
way that we used to.

01:29:49.578 --> 01:29:53.278
- So speaking of which, Steve,
you told us a story about

01:29:53.758 --> 01:29:57.538
soup- ... that made you maybe fall
